I'm not a lawyer, but I was under the impression that Judges decided
sentences. Juries decide whether a defendant is guilty or innocent.

At best, you're come up with an argument that Judges shouldn't read
pornography *if* you suppose that a higher sentence is more "right"
than a lower one. I suspect that Judges would be much more likely to
take various rules into account (whatever they'd been reading) than
laymen who weren't aware of such rules.

~If I were convinced that a man who raped a woman would, on average,
~face a sentence which most people would consider fair for a man who
