Pornography is generally not illegal; indeed it is protected by the
First Amendment. The general idea is that that as sovereign citizens
of a democratic republic, we can read pretty much what we like becuase
the government cannot be trust to decide what to ban.


"Obscenity" can be illegal; I'm enclosing information. If your concern
is that government funds are being used to transmit this material, I
would point own that _Penthouse_ is distributed over government roads
and that most state universities *pay* to subscribe to _Playboy_.  The
general idea is that libraries and networks should have a diversity of
information. The extreme alternative, to ban anything that anyone
objects to, would mean that almost nothing would be allowed in
libraries or on networks since somebody objects to almost everything.

- Carl

