We've dealt with this issue with K-12 access and have decided that it is an
education issue, not a University censorship issue.  We have taken pains to
make the school aware of the risks, of what kids can get into if they are not
monitored, and we have worked with the school to educate children and parents
concerning responsible behavior on networks.  Since we've been working with
middle school children whose network access is closely monitored by teachers
and restricted to classroom time, we have not had problems.  But I believe is
is just as much the classroom teacher's responsibility to monitor what comes
into the classroom electronically as it is in any other medium.

