Not my responsibility.  I'm not trying to be facetious, either; such reports
are rarely published here.  An e-mail request to help@cac.washington.edu might
get you a copy, via surface mail, of the current UW Guide to Computing, which
includes the official policy statement on acceptable use and lists the members
of the UACAC (computing advisory committee).  As far as I know, this document
is not on-line.  There is also a new gopher server here, I think it's
gopher.u.washington.edu.  Beyond that, I think it's up to EFF to submit a FOI
request to the university if it wants more details.

>>At the UW, even "Playboy" is kept behind the counter, so to speak.
