[This is the U. of Washington acceptable use statement.]

 Everyone within the UW community who uses a computer,
 whether it is a PC, a workstation, or a multi-user
 computer, has the responsibility to use the resources in an
 ethical and legal manner. This means that users agree to
 abide by the following conditions:
 
 o The integrity of the systems must be respected.
 
 o Privacy of other users must not be intruded upon at any
   time. (For example, do not send email to someone who has
   requested that you not do so.)
 
 o The rules and regulations governing the use of UW
   facilities and equipment must be respected.

 o No one will obtain unauthorized access to other users'
   accounts and files.
 
 o The intended use of all computer accounts, for University
   research, instruction, and administrative purposes, must be
   respected.
 
 In summary, when you are using computers at the UW,
 University policy prohibits account theft, file theft,
 violations of informational privacy, and/or penetration or
 harm to operating systems. If abuse of computer systems
 occurs, those responsible for such abuse will be held
 legally accountable.
